# language-frontend — a frontend for a small but real imperative language.
#
# This is the "host your language on Capy" shape, in one file. It is not a
# config DSL or a template: it is a grammar with nested scopes, typed
# parameter lists, recursive expressions and statement-level recovery.
#
#   fn NAME(P: T, …) { … }    named nonterminal for the parameter list
#   let NAME = EXPR           a whole expression in one `any` capture
#   if EXPR { … }             nested block scope
#   while EXPR { … }          nested block scope
#   return EXPR
#   NAME(ARGS)                a call statement
#
# Two things make it a frontend rather than a template:
#
#   1. `capy ast` gives you the tree — every node spanned, blocks nested,
#      the parameter list a real sub-tree rather than a flat string.
#   2. Parsing RECOVERS, so a file with several mistakes yields the tree of
#      what parsed plus one diagnostic per bad region. That is what a
#      language's users need from its error messages.
#
# The `write` templates lower it to Python, to show the frontend is attached
# to something. Lowering is optional — a consumer that only wants the tree
# never calls `capy run` at all.
extension ml

# --- the parameter list: a named nonterminal, not a flat token run ---

function param
    arg capture pname ident
    arg literal ":"
    arg capture ptype ident
    write `${pname}: ${ptype}`
end

# --- declarations ---

function fn
    arg literal "fn"
    arg capture name ident
    arg literal "("
    arg capture params param* sep "," join ", "
    arg literal ")"
    block_open "{" close "}"
    write `def ${name}(${params}):
${indent 4 body}
`
end

# --- statements ---

function let
    arg literal "let"
    arg capture name ident
    arg literal "="
    arg capture value any
    write `${name} = ${value}
`
end

function if
    arg literal "if"
    arg capture cond any
    block_open "{" close "}"
    write `if ${cond}:
${indent 4 body}`
end

function while
    arg literal "while"
    arg capture cond any
    block_open "{" close "}"
    write `while ${cond}:
${indent 4 body}`
end

function return
    arg literal "return"
    arg capture value any
    write `return ${value}
`
end
